<title>CHINA: Sanwa Bank opens Shanghai Pudong branch.</title>
<headline>Sanwa Bank opens Shanghai Pudong branch.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Sanwa Bank, one of nine foreign banks so far approved to do local Chinese yuan business, has opened a branch in Shanghai's Pudong development zone, the Shanghai Securities News said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>China's central bank has given approval to the foreign banks to conduct local currency business on the condition that they move their main Shanghai branch to the Pudong district, which the city wants to make into a major financial centre.</p>
</text>
